github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-12T14:57:43Z","updated_at":"2025-04-12T15:04:09Z","body":"> Just calling NavigationRegion2D.get_rid() caused it to crash\n\nIt is the string format that makes things explode, not the get_rid() function. Without the string format it does not crash in Godot 4.1.1 and also not crash in Godot master. I just tested it with both versions and both your provided script as well as with all navigation related nodes that have a get_rid() function.\n\nI think this should be kept open. The GDScript string format should never crash the engine when trying to string format a RID, it should error out. Ideally it should also auto convert to string when used in that script context with a RID used in a format string.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2798863167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2798866306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105315#issuecomment-2798866306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105315